Package: metacleaner
Type: Package
Title: Automated Curation of DNA Barcode Reference Databases
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sean", "Bresnahan", email = "seantbresnahan3@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
    )
Description: Removes mislabeled and contaminant sequences from DNA barcode
    reference databases used in metabarcoding and metagenomics, such as plant
    internal transcribed spacer (ITS1/ITS2) databases built from 'NCBI'
    'GenBank' records. Query sequences are searched against a database of
    unwanted sequences (for example fungi) and a database of wanted sequences
    (for example plants) with a built-in k-mer seeded, multithreaded alignment
    engine written in C++ (or optionally with 'BLAST+'), and sequences whose best matches
    disagree with their own taxonomy at a chosen rank are flagged and removed.
    Taxonomy can come from a local table, from 'NCBI' web services, or from a
    'taxonomizr' database. Helper functions download, tidy and de-replicate
    reference sequences from 'NCBI'. The method was used in Crone et al. (2023)
    <doi:10.1002/ece3.10640>.
License: GPL-3
URL: https://seantbresnahan.com/metacleaner/,
    https://github.com/sbresnahan/metacleaner
BugReports: https://github.com/sbresnahan/metacleaner/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: parallel, Rcpp, stats, utils
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Suggests: knitr, rentrez, rmarkdown, taxonomizr, testthat (>= 3.0.0),
        xml2
SystemRequirements: BLAST+ (optional; only needed for engine = "blast")
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Language: en-US
